From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a shared leaderboard and photo faces
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Leaderboard
- api/scores.js: Vercel function backed by Upstash Redis (REST, no npm
  packages). GET returns the top names per board (all, zen, riki, koska)
  and where a given name stands; POST saves a finished shift.
- Each name is ranked by its best shift; every run is also logged.
- Scores are checked for plausibility against bars caught, and saves are
  limited to 20 per minute per address.
- Shift report asks for a name once, then saves every shift with points
  automatically, and shows the top five. New leaderboard screen with a
  tab per inmate. Scores that can't be sent wait on the device and go out
  on the next visit. With no API or database the leaderboard stays hidden.

Photo faces
- Zen, Riki, Koska and Mällu get bobblehead photo faces (faces/*.webp),
  with body skin tinted to match. Heads bob while running, swell on a
  catch and flash red on a hit.

README covers turning the leaderboard on in Vercel (Upstash for Redis).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
